# Handheld method catalog

`handheld/lib/methods.g.dart` is generated from the Go method table. CI compares them in `TestMethodCatalogMatchesClient`. A new or renamed method without a regenerated catalog fails that test.

## Same turn

If you add, rename, or remove a `case` in `internal/api/rpc.go`, `internal/app/video.go`, or `internal/remote/node.go`, regenerate the catalog before the task is done. The Dart file belongs in the same change as the Go case.

From the `yoyo` module root, in PowerShell:

```powershell
$env:YOYO_WRITE_METHODS='1'; go test ./internal/remote/ -run TestMethodCatalogMatchesClient -count=1; Remove-Item Env:YOYO_WRITE_METHODS
go test ./internal/remote/ -run TestMethodCatalogMatchesClient -count=1
```

The second run must pass with the variable unset. Do not hand-edit `methods.g.dart`.

## What the scanner sees

Only tab-indented `case` lines in those three files. A method name is the quoted string. Fields come from `json:"..."` tags and `str("...")` arguments in that case body. Names sort alphabetically into the Dart list.
